# Moving resources between containers (LWS 1.0 core sections 6.1.3, 7, 9.6 and 10.2.2).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: "LWS 1.0 core: moving resources between containers"
comment: >-
  The 19 October 2026 draft lets a client move a resource to another container by changing the
  up link in its linkset with JSON Patch (w3c/lws-protocol#237). A storage that allows it says
  so with a MoveResource capability in its storage description, whose appliesTo says whether
  containers move too and whose preservesIdentifier says whether a moved resource keeps its
  URI; one that does not must refuse the change. Each test reads the storage description first
  and applies only to the storages its precondition describes. A move patch replaces
  /linkset/0/up/0/href, which assumes that the resource's own link context is the first in its
  linkset and its up link the first target: the draft's own examples do, and a test whose
  linkset is laid out otherwise does not apply. Every patch is conditional on the linkset's
  current ETag, as clients SHOULD make it.
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/
entries:

  - id: "#discovery-move-capability"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: discovery-move-capability
    label: A MoveResource capability's appliesTo and preservesIdentifier are well formed
    comment: >-
      "appliesTo - the appliesTo property is OPTIONAL. If present, its value MUST be a set of
      strings naming the types of Storage Resource the capability applies to, such as
      DataResource or Container." "preservesIdentifier - ... If present, its value MUST be a
      boolean." A set of strings is a JSON array of them; a Storage Resource type is
      DataResource or Container, by its term or its IRI.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#storage-description-capabilities
    traits: [Get, Discovery, StorageDescription]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/capability-move-applies-to
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/capability-move-preserves-identifier
    steps:
      - label: the storage describes a MoveResource capability (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
      - label: its appliesTo, if any, is a set of Storage Resource types, and its preservesIdentifier a boolean
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
                - pointer: /appliesTo
                  optional: true
                  jsonType: array
                - pointer: /appliesTo
                  optional: true
                  every:
                    - pointer: ""
                      matches: '^(https://www\.w3\.org/ns/lws#)?(DataResource|Container)$'
                - pointer: /preservesIdentifier
                  optional: true
                  jsonType: boolean

  - id: "#move-data-resource"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: move-data-resource
    label: Patching a data resource's up link moves it to the other container
    comment: >-
      A client "moves a resource by applying a partial update to the resource's linkset
      resource, replacing the target of the up link with the identifier of the destination
      container", which servers that describe MoveResource must accept as JSON Patch. "On a
      successful update, the server MUST atomically remove the resource from the items list of
      its former parent container and add it to the items list of the destination container."
      Whether the moved resource keeps its URI is the storage's choice, so the destination is
      checked for one data resource rather than for the old URI. The linkset must show the up
      link the patch replaces: that is how a client learns its position.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#containment-integrity
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, DataResource, Container]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-server-support
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-request-json-patch
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-containment-atomic
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/containment-integrity-move
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/capability-move-resource
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: source
        - container: destination
        - dataResource: moved
          in: source
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource on the move
    steps:
      - label: the storage describes a MoveResource capability (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the linkset shows the up link to its container
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset
              some:
                - pointer: /anchor
                  equalsIri: "${moved}"
                - pointer: /up
                  some:
                    - pointer: /href
                      equalsIri: "${source}"
      - label: the resource's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${source}"
      - label: replace the up link with the destination
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: the destination lists one data resource
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${destination}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              count: 1
            - pointer: /items/0/type
              hasValue: DataResource
      - label: and the container it left lists nothing
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${source}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              equals: []

  - id: "#move-updates-container-etags"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: move-updates-container-etags
    label: A move changes the ETag of the container left and of the container joined
    comment: >-
      On a successful move, "the ETag of both containers MUST be updated to reflect the change."
      Each container's tag is read before the move and must differ after it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, Container, Conditional]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-containment-atomic
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: source
        - container: destination
        - dataResource: moved
          in: source
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource on the move
    steps:
      - label: the storage describes a MoveResource capability (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
      - label: the container it is in has an ETag
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${source}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              capture: sourceTag
      - label: and so has the destination
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${destination}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              capture: destinationTag
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the resource's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${source}"
      - label: move it
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: the container it left has a new ETag
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${source}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              differsFrom: "${sourceTag}"
      - label: and so has the container it joined
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${destination}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              differsFrom: "${destinationTag}"

  - id: "#move-keeps-identifier-content-and-links"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: move-keeps-identifier-content-and-links
    label: A storage that preserves identifiers keeps a moved resource's URI, content and links
    comment: >-
      A storage whose MoveResource says preservesIdentifier true says that it "preserves the
      identifier of a moved resource", which servers SHOULD do so that links to it stay valid.
      Whatever it does with identifiers, "The content of the moved resource and its
      user-defined metadata are unaffected by the move", and "Servers MUST preserve the links
      in the linkset resource that the client is not permitted to modify". The resource gets a
      license link before it moves; afterwards its old URI answers with the same content, an up
      link to the destination and its type, and its linkset still holds the license.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#storage-description-capabilities
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, DataResource]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-identifier-preserved
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/capability-move-preserves-identifier
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-preserves-content-and-links
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: source
        - container: destination
        - dataResource: moved
          in: source
          contentType: text/plain
          body: content that travels unchanged
    steps:
      - label: the storage's MoveResource says it preserves identifiers (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
                - pointer: /preservesIdentifier
                  equals: true
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the resource's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${source}"
      - label: give it a license link (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: add
              path: /linkset/0/license
              value:
                - href: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: move it
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: its URI answers with the same content, linked up to the destination
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: up
              href: "${destination}"
            - rel: type
              href: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#DataResource
          bodyMatches: '^content that travels unchanged$'
      - label: the destination lists it by that URI
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${destination}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${moved}"
      - label: its linkset still holds the license
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset
              some:
                - pointer: /license
                  some:
                    - pointer: /href
                      equals: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  - id: "#move-invalid-destination-refused"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: move-invalid-destination-refused
    label: A move to anything but an existing container, or away from every container, is refused
    comment: >-
      "The destination MUST be an existing container. Servers MUST reject a patch that would set
      the target of the up link to anything other than an existing container with an
      appropriate 4xx status code ... Servers MUST likewise reject a patch that would leave the
      resource without an up link." Three patches are tried: one to a container that does not
      exist, one to a data resource, and one removing the up link. Each is refused, and the
      resource stays where it was.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, DataResource]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-destination-existing-container
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: nowhere
          absent: true
        - dataResource: notContainer
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a data resource is no container
        - dataResource: moved
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource that stays put
    steps:
      - label: the storage describes a MoveResource capability (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the resource's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${test.container}"
      - label: a move into a container that does not exist is refused
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${nowhere}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a move into a data resource is refused
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${notContainer}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: removing the up link is refused
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: remove
              path: /linkset/0/up
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: the resource is still in the test container
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: up
              href: "${test.container}"

  - id: "#move-container"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: move-container
    label: A storage that moves containers moves one, with what it holds
    comment: >-
      "Servers MAY support changing the up link of a container, and MUST indicate that they do
      so by including Container in the appliesTo property of the MoveResource capability. When
      a container is moved, its descendants move with it." The moved container holds a data
      resource; afterwards the destination holds one container, which holds one data resource,
      and the container left holds nothing.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#storage-description-capabilities
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, Container]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-containers-applies-to
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/capability-move-applies-to
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-containment-atomic
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: source
        - container: destination
        - container: moved
          in: source
        - dataResource: inner
          in: moved
          contentType: text/plain
          body: carried along
    steps:
      - label: the storage moves containers (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
                - pointer: /appliesTo
                  hasValue: Container
      - label: find the container's linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the container's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${source}"
      - label: move it
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: the destination lists one container
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${destination}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              count: 1
            - pointer: /items/0/type
              hasValue: Container
            - pointer: /items/0/id
              capture: arrived
      - label: which still holds the data resource
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${arrived}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              count: 1
            - pointer: /items/0/type
              hasValue: DataResource
      - label: and the container it left lists nothing
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${source}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              equals: []

  - id: "#move-container-into-itself-refused"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: move-container-into-itself-refused
    label: A container cannot be moved into itself or into a container it holds
    comment: >-
      "In particular, a container MUST NOT be moved into itself or into one of its own
      descendants, as this would introduce a cycle in the containment hierarchy", and such an
      update is rejected with a 4xx. Only a storage that moves containers is asked; one that
      does not refuses any container move, which move-container-refused-without-container-support
      checks.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#security-moving-resources
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, Container]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-containment-integrity-cycles
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: outer
        - container: inner
          in: outer
    steps:
      - label: the storage moves containers (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
                - pointer: /appliesTo
                  hasValue: Container
      - label: find the outer container's linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${outer}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the container's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${outer}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${test.container}"
      - label: a move into the container it holds is refused
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${inner}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a move into itself is refused
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${outer}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: the outer container is still in the test container
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${test.container}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${outer}"
      - label: and still holds the inner one
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${outer}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${inner}"

  - id: "#move-container-refused-without-container-support"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: move-container-refused-without-container-support
    label: A storage whose MoveResource leaves out Container refuses to move a container
    comment: >-
      "If the property is absent, the capability applies to data resources only", and "A server
      that supports moving data resources but not containers MUST reject such a request with an
      appropriate 4xx status code, such as 409 Conflict, and MUST NOT include Container in the
      appliesTo property." The test applies to a storage whose MoveResource has no appliesTo,
      or one without Container.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#storage-description-capabilities
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, Container]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-containers-applies-to
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/capability-move-applies-to
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: destination
        - container: moved
    steps:
      - label: the storage moves data resources but not containers (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
                - pointer: /appliesTo
                  optional: true
                  none:
                    - pointer: ""
                      matches: '^(https://www\.w3\.org/ns/lws#)?Container$'
      - label: find the container's linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the container's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${test.container}"
      - label: moving the container is refused
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: the container is still in the test container
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: up
              href: "${test.container}"

  - id: "#move-refused-without-capability"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: move-refused-without-capability
    label: A storage that describes no MoveResource capability refuses to move a resource
    comment: >-
      "A server that does not allow it MUST reject the request with an appropriate 4xx status
      code, such as 409 Conflict, and MUST NOT describe a MoveResource capability." The test
      applies to a storage that describes none, and points a data resource's up link at another
      container that exists, so the refusal can only be for the move itself.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#storage-description-capabilities
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, DataResource]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-server-support
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/capability-move-resource
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: destination
        - dataResource: moved
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource that stays put
    steps:
      - label: the storage describes no MoveResource capability (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              optional: true
              none:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: point its up link at the other container, which is refused
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: add
              path: /linkset/0/up
              value:
                - href: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: the resource is still in the test container
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: up
              href: "${test.container}"
      - label: and the other container is empty
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${destination}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              equals: []

  - id: "#move-needs-create-in-destination"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: move-needs-create-in-destination
    label: An agent who may not create in the destination cannot move a resource there
    comment: >-
      "A server MUST NOT apply a change to an up link unless the requesting agent is authorized
      both to perform the delete resource operation on the resource being moved and to perform
      the create resource operation in the destination container." bob may read, modify and
      delete the resource, and read the destination, but not create in it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#security-moving-resources
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, DataResource, Authz, AccessGrants]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-authorization-delete-and-create
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/security-move-privilege-combination
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: destination
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
        - dataResource: moved
          contentType: text/plain
          body: bob may delete this, not put it there
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
            modify: [bob]
            delete: [bob]
    steps:
      - label: the storage describes a MoveResource capability (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
      - label: bob finds its linkset
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the resource's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${test.container}"
      - label: bob's move into the destination is refused
        as: bob
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: the destination is still empty
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${destination}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              equals: []

  - id: "#move-needs-delete-of-resource"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: move-needs-delete-of-resource
    label: An agent who may not delete a resource cannot move it
    comment: >-
      The other half of the rule move-needs-create-in-destination checks: bob may read and
      modify the resource and create in the destination, but not delete the resource. Without
      the delete, a move would let him take a resource out of a container he cannot delete from
      (section 16.6, "Privilege Combination").
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#security-moving-resources
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, DataResource, Authz, AccessGrants]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-authorization-delete-and-create
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/security-move-privilege-combination
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: destination
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
            create: [bob]
        - dataResource: moved
          contentType: text/plain
          body: bob may change this, not take it away
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
            modify: [bob]
    steps:
      - label: the storage describes a MoveResource capability (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
      - label: bob finds its linkset
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the resource's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${test.container}"
      - label: bob's move into the destination is refused
        as: bob
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: the resource is still in the test container
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: up
              href: "${test.container}"

  - id: "#move-notification"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: move-notification
    label: A move is announced as one Move activity from the container left to the container joined
    comment: >-
      A server that allows moves "MUST support the following activity type: Move ... The origin
      field indicates the container from which the resource was removed, and the target field
      indicates the container into which it was added", and "SHOULD describe a successful move
      with a single Move activity ... rather than with a separate Delete and Create activity."
      A subscription to the test container, which holds both containers, hears the move.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#activity-types
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261019/#moving-resources
    traits: [Patch, Get, Linkset, Notifications]
    requires: [ReachableFixtures]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/notification-activity-move
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/move-notification-single-activity
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: source
        - container: destination
        - dataResource: moved
          in: source
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource on the move
    steps:
      - label: the storage moves resources and offers webhook subscriptions (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /capability
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: MoveResource
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: NotificationService
                - pointer: /subscriptionType
                  hasValue: WebhookSubscription
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${moved}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the resource's link context comes first, and its up link first in it (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset/0/anchor
              equalsIri: "${moved}"
            - pointer: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              equalsIri: "${source}"
      - label: subscribe to the test container
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.NotificationService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: WebhookSubscription
            topic: ["${test.container}"]
            inbox: "${test.inbox}"
        response:
          statusCode: "2xx"
          json:
            - pointer: /subscription
              jsonType: string
              capture: subscription
      - label: move the resource
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/json-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            - op: replace
              path: /linkset/0/up/0/href
              value: "${destination}"
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: a Notification announcing the Move arrives
        as: anonymous
        poll: {within: 30, every: 2}
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${test.inbox}"
          accept: application/json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /deliveries
              some:
                - pointer: /activities
                  some:
                    - pointer: /type
                      hasValue: Move
                    - pointer: /origin
                      equalsIri: "${source}"
                    - pointer: /target
                      equalsIri: "${destination}"
      - label: cancel the subscription (tidying up, not judged)
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${subscription}"
        response:
          statusCode: ["2xx", "4xx"]
